From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:26:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #3903] mcs51: compare addresses of banked functions
 without an internal error

With --model-huge every function is banked and its address is three bytes.
Comparisons of such addresses go through sdcc_gptr_cmp, and
loadDptrFromOperand asserted ("need pointerCode") when the left operand was
the immediate address of a function, because it only knew how to produce the
third byte for a generic pointer made by a cast. For a banked function that
byte is simply the bank, the top byte of the address.

Re-enables tests/funcptrcmp.c.in for mcs51.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mcs51/gen.c                          | 5 +++++
 support/regression/tests/funcptrcmp.c.in | 2 --
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mcs51/gen.c b/src/mcs51/gen.c
index 9189ad43f..de1c29cfe 100644
--- a/src/mcs51/gen.c
+++ b/src/mcs51/gen.c
@@ -2072,6 +2072,11 @@ loadDptrFromOperand (operand *op, bool loadBToo)
             {
               if (AOP (op)->aopu.aop_immd.from_cast_remat)
                 emitcode ("mov", "b,%s", opGet (op, AOP_SIZE (op) - 1, FALSE, FALSE));
+              else if (IFFUNC_ISBANKEDCALL (operandType (op)))
+                {
+                  /* The address of a banked function: the third byte is its bank, not a pointer type. */
+                  emitcode ("mov", "b,%s", opGet (op, AOP_SIZE (op) - 1, FALSE, FALSE));
+                }
               else
                 {
                   wassertl (FALSE, "need pointerCode");
diff --git a/support/regression/tests/funcptrcmp.c.in b/support/regression/tests/funcptrcmp.c.in
index d00f51411..ad4c76aa9 100644
--- a/support/regression/tests/funcptrcmp.c.in
+++ b/support/regression/tests/funcptrcmp.c.in
@@ -35,9 +35,7 @@
 void
 testFuncPtrCmp(void)
 {
-#ifndef __SDCC_mcs51 // bug #3903
 	ASSERT (&f1 != &g1);
 	ASSERT (&f2 != &g2);
-#endif
 }
 
